The sinking of the save of the link register.

The retail's compiler lets the scheduler sink the save of the link register
into the body of the function: in most of its functions the store is not
the second instruction but the fourth, the fifth or the sixth, after the
load of a global or the copy of an argument.  GCC 4.1 marks that store as
frame related, which forbids the scheduler to move it, so the store stays
in the prologue.

This patch clears the flag on that one store and adds the option that
controls it.  The retail's behaviour is the default; -mno-ps3-lr-sink
keeps the one of GCC 4.1.

The files it touches - gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c and
gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.opt - are upstream GNU Compiler Collection, and
each carries the Free Software Foundation's notice:

    This file is part of GCC.  GCC is free software; you can redistribute
    it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public
    License as published by the Free Software Foundation; either version
    2, or (at your option) any later version.

A modification of a GPL file is under the GPL, so this patch is published
under the same terms, with the notices kept.  It touches no file that Sony
added to GCC, and quotes no SDK header, library or sample.
diff --git a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
index 8c8f594..cbdf375 100755
--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
@@ -16120,6 +16120,15 @@ rs6000_emit_prologue (void)
       insn = emit_move_insn (mem, reg);
       rs6000_frame_related (insn, frame_ptr_rtx, info->total_size,
 			    NULL_RTX, NULL_RTX);
+      /* The retail's compiler lets the scheduler sink the save of the
+	 link register into the body of the function: in most of its
+	 functions the store is not the second instruction but the fourth,
+	 the fifth or the sixth.  GCC 4.1 marks the store as frame related,
+	 which forbids the scheduler to move it.  Clearing the flag
+	 restores the retail's behaviour; -mno-ps3-lr-sink keeps the one
+	 of GCC 4.1.  */
+      if (ps3_lr_sink)
+	RTX_FRAME_RELATED_P (insn) = 0;
     }
 
   /* Save CR if we use any that must be preserved.  */
diff --git a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.opt b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.opt
index f20e7f0..b3f62e7 100755
--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.opt
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.opt
@@ -325,3 +325,11 @@ Read the entry of the TOC in one instruction, from r2.
 mps3-neg-disp
 Target Var(ps3_neg_disp) Init(0)
 Fold a negative displacement into the load.
+
+; The retail's compiler lets the scheduler sink the save of the link
+; register into the body of the function; GCC 4.1 marks the store as frame
+; related, which forbids it.  The retail's behaviour is the default here;
+; -mno-ps3-lr-sink keeps the one of GCC 4.1.
+mps3-lr-sink
+Target Var(ps3_lr_sink) Init(1)
+Let the scheduler sink the save of the link register into the body.
